    "post": "💡 Claude Design for UX Design\n\nClaude Design is a very nice tool for quick prototyping. It helps you turn your idea into an interactive prototype in no time. But you can do much more with this tool by taking a different approach: focus on user experience.\n \nHere is a 3-step UX-first workflow for Claude Design:\n \n1️⃣ Generate a complete UX flow, not just UI screens\n \nBy asking Claude to design an experience, you will make AI invest more effort in building a solid user experience, not just nice-looking screens. As a result, the output AI generates won’t be a generic prototype; it will be a prototype aligned with your user’s needs and wants.\n \n \n2️⃣ Ask it to explain design decisions\n \nOnce you've generated a design with Claude, you might notice unclear areas (where it's not clear why the AI designed the UI this way). Instead of guessing, you can ask Claude to dig into a particular area and provide a more detailed explanation of the design decision.\n \n \n3️⃣ Turn an existing UI into a design artifact\n \nYou can ask Claude Design to reverse-engineer a design it generated for you (i.e., match the generated design to your design system’s styles and components).\n\n \n📕 Complete guide for UX Design with Claude Design: https://lnkd.in/em2Vt6BS \n \n\n #claude #claudedesign #ai #aidesign #productdesign #ux #uxdesign",
