    "height": 405,
    "post": "Claude Code + Figma Design System = ❤️\n\nClaude Code can now generate UI design in Figma using your design system.\n\nAnd the great thing is that you can do it in 3 simple steps:\n\nStep 1️⃣: Publish your design system in Figma &  ask Claude Code to analyze it\n\nCreate an empty Claude Code project and submit the following prompt in it:\n\nPrompt template:\n[LINK to Figma File with your DS] This is a design system I will use for this project. Analyze it and provide a summary of your analysis.\n\nWhat will happen:\nClaude Code will analyse your design system and add essential details about it to the current context. \n\nQuick note: \nMake sure you have Figma MCP installed in your Claude Code.\n\nStep 2️⃣ : Provide a link to an empty Figma file & ask Claude Code to generate  UI design for you\n\nPrompt template:\n[slash]figma-generate-design [WHAT YOU WANT CLAUDE TO CREATE] [LINK TO FIGMA WORK FILE]\n\nWhat will happen:\nClaude Code will generate a design in real time using styles and UI components from the design system you’ve provided, and send the UI design to the Figma work file.\n\nStep 3️⃣: Refine your design in Figma & ask Claude to Code it \n\nYou can refine your design in Figma by making direct edits or updating the styles/components in your design system. Once you're satisfied with your edits, you can ask Claude Code to code your design:\n\nPrompt template:\n[LINK TO SELECTION in FIGMA] code this design [REQUIREMENTS FOR CODE]\n\nWhat will happen:\nClaude Code will reach Figma for the design and use it as a reference when coding the page/screen.  \n\nQuick note: The coded version of your design won’t be a 1:1 translation from design to code. Claude Code may introduce some changes along the way.\n\n📕 Complete step-by-step guide: https://lnkd.in/e8gmafcQ \n\n#AI #claude #claudecode #design #figma #figmaAI",
