    "post": "Heyy designers 👋🏼 So.. Claude can read every comment in your Figma file and turn them into a clear list of what the team actually needs to do. I tested it this week and it's pretty cool!\n\nComments are where half our decisions get made, but they're a nightmare to track. You leave some, a teammate leaves some, the client leaves some, and they all just sit there as orange dots scattered across the canvas. No overview of what's still open, what got answered, or where two people quietly disagree about the same thing.\n\nSo I pointed Claude at the whole file through the Figma Console MCP (the bridge that lets Claude reach into your Figma file and actually pull things out, instead of just looking at a screenshot of it).\n\nI asked it to sort everything into what the team needs to do. What needs a decision, what's an open question and who it's waiting on, what's a to-do and who owns it, what's already resolved. It even catches when two people leave conflicting takes on the same element and flags it as something that needs a call...(cause you know there's always that..)\n\nIf you use n8n (a tool for automating steps between your apps), you can wire this to run on its own. Every morning it re-reads the file and drops the update into a Notion board or a Slack channel, or whatever else you use, so the whole team sees what moved since yesterday without anyone opening Figma...\n\nOh and you can also have Claude leave comments for you in Figma directly based on your convo!\n\nI'm testing this with a real client team this week and will share more results of the entire workflow.\n\nAs usualllll, follow for more AI tips 😁\n\n#claude #ai #design #figma #ux",
